            ],
            "rationale": "The per-member balance rule (fines less payments) stays in Tier 2 (Accounts.owed), and Tier 3 calls it. But the new library-wide derivation 'total all members owe' is defined in the Tier 3 Views module, and it decides locally which members count: those that appear in the fines list. That partly re-derives a balance rule outside Tier 1/2. It does not contradict Tier 2, because a member with no fines adds nothing there. The no-overwrite guard for backups is also decided in Tier 3, though that is closer to an I/O policy than a lending rule. The CLI now only dispatches and renders.",
            "score": 1
